Description: GullDesk OS desktop appearance and shell
 This package carries the GullDesk OS desktop: a complete Material 3 design
 for Plasma, generated from one seed colour.
 .
  * the GullDesk Dark and Light colour schemes and the GullDesk Plasma theme,
    drawn from the same Material 3 palette;
  * the GullDesk icon theme, drawn from Material Symbols Rounded;
  * GullDesk Launcher, an application menu with search, and GullDesk Quick
    Settings, the status area and the shade pulled up from the panel;
  * GullDesk Shapes, a live wallpaper of Material 3 Expressive shapes;
  * the GullDesk Kvantum theme, which gives every Qt widget -- menus,
    buttons, fields, lists -- the same Material shapes and palette;
  * a Qt Quick Controls style for System Settings and other QML applications,
    and the GullDesk window decoration;
  * the splash and the look-and-feel package that lays out the floating
    panel and selects all of the above.
 .
 It sets that look-and-feel as the system-wide default, so a freshly
 created account starts with the GullDesk desktop instead of the Plasma one.

Package: gulldesk-calamares
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 calamares (>= 3.3.14-1gulldesk3),
 gulldesk-desktop (= ${source:Version}),
 pkexec,
 polkitd
Description: GullDesk OS installer configuration
 This package configures Calamares to install GullDesk OS from the live image
 onto a disk: the module sequence, the target clean-up of live-only settings
 and the GullDesk installer branding.
 .
 The installer removes this package while installing, which leaves Calamares
 without a configuration on the installed system.
